'''Zorii Bliss''', also known as '''Zorii Wynn''', was a [[human]] [[Gender|female]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the frigid [[planet]] [[Kijimi]]. She was the leader of the [[Spice Runners of Kijimi]]. During the [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]], Bliss was neutral, and she spent [[time]] in Kijimi's [[Thieves' Quarter]]. She shared a past connection with [[Poe Dameron]] as he was once a spice runner along with her, but Poe Dameron [[Kijimi summit|left the group]] and abandoned Bliss. The two would meet again when Dameron [[Mission to Kijimi|led]] Resistance operatives to Kijimi to find the hidden world [[Exegol]]. After the [[destruction of Kijimi]], Bliss participated in the [[Battle of Exegol]], which saw the destruction of the [[Sith Eternal]]'s fleet, the [[Final Order]].

==Biography==
===Spice Running===
{{Quote|Then run! Run for your life, Poe&mdash;and don't ever come back.|Zorii Bliss orders Poe Dameron after he rejects her offer to take over the Spice Runners|<ref name="Free Fall" />}}
[[File:ZoriiBliss-TROSposter.png|thumb|left|200px|Zorii Bliss led a group of Spice Runners.]]
[[Reproduction|Born]] Between [[1 BBY]] and [[1 ABY]],<ref name="Zorii birth" /> Zorii Bliss, also known as Zorii Wynn,<ref name="Free Fall" /> was a resident of the frigid planet [[Kijimi]]<ref name="TROSVD" /> who joined the [[Spice Runners of Kijimi]], a criminal organization run by her [[Reproduction|mother]] [[Zeva Bliss]], at a young age.<ref name="Free Fall" /> Zeva had succeeded [[Zarah Bliss]] as the group's leader during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="The Rebellion 1">[[Return of the Jedi – The Rebellion 1|''Return of the Jedi – The Rebellion'' 1]]</ref>

[[Poe Dameron]] later joined the Spice Runners. However, Poe abandoned the group<ref name="TROSVD" /> during the [[Kijimi summit]]&mdash;rejecting Zorii's offer to take over the pirates from her mother<ref name="Free Fall" />&mdash;to return home and later join the [[New Republic]] as a [[T-85 X-wing starfighter|T-85 X-wing]] [[pilot]]. He then joined the [[Resistance]] as a [[T-70 X-wing starfighter|T-70 X-wing]] pilot, following in the footsteps of his parents [[Shara Bey]] and [[Kes Dameron]], both of whom fought for the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebellion]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="TROSVD" /> Poe's departure greatly angered Bliss,<ref name="Free Fall" /> as well as many others on Kijimi that Poe had run afoul of.<ref name="Episode IX" /> At some point before the [[Cold War]], Bliss succeeded in becoming leader of the spice runners.<ref name="TROSVD" />

===First Order-Resistance War===
In the years that followed, the [[First Order]], a military organization built on the ashes of the [[Galactic Empire]] seized control of Kijimi, abducting people and following the [[Battle of Crait]], took control of the world, as they had with many other planets across the galaxy. Zorii and the others learned to operate under the new control without Dameron. Unable to stand the cries she heard everywhere, however, she plotted to leave Kijimi<ref name="Episode IX" /> and purchased a [[BTA-NR2 Y-wing starfighter]] for about 40,000 [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]], naming the ship the ''[[Comeuppance]]'' on the belief she had many scores to settle.<ref name="TROS Expanded">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref>

[[File:ZoriiBliss2-TROS.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Bliss confronts Poe Dameron on Kijimi.]]
When the [[Resistance]] [[agent]]s [[Mission to Kijimi|arrived]] on Kijimi in [[35 ABY]] to find the path to [[Exegol]], Bliss confronted Dameron, alongside a group of goons, still furious at the pilot over his abandonment of their cause, but [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] knocked out her goons, Bliss was impressed by her skill, and was convinced to help them. Bliss then led them to [[Babu Frik]], the legendary droidsmith, as the Resistance needed to unlock forbidden translations in the systems of [[C-3PO]], in order to translate a [[Blade of Ochi of Bestoon|dagger]] that would lead to a [[Emperor's wayfinder|wayfinder]] to the hidden world Exegol. Bliss and Dameron left the room while Frik was working, and spied on First Order operations from the roof of the workshop, talking about how the occupation changed things. During the conversation, Bliss reassured and motivated Dameron to continue the fight against the First Order, and removed part of her helmet.<ref name="Episode IX" />

The pair then altered the other Resistance agents to approaching First Order forces. Understanding that Poe needed to get on board Kylo Ren's [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer]], Zorii gives him a captain's medallion at great cost. As they began their escape, now with the added knowledge that their [[Wookiee]] friend [[Chewbacca]] was being held on the First Order capital ship [[Steadfast (Resurgent-class)|''Steadfast'']], Poe made an offer to Bliss for her to join them, which she declined. Bliss then remained on Kijimi while Poe and his allies liberated Chewbacca, before traveling to [[Kef Bir]] after translating the dagger.<ref name="Episode IX" />

====Battle of Exegol====
[[File:Comeuppance2-SWGOH.png|thumb|left|250px|Zorii Bliss pilots the ''Comeuppance'' at Exegol.]]
The resurrected [[Darth Sidious]] soon gave the order to use [[Derriphan|one]] of his [[Xyston-class Star Destroyer|''Xyston''-class Star Destroyers]] to destroy a planet that the Resistance would know. Kijimi was chosen, and subsequently obliterated by the Star Destroyer's [[axial superlaser]].<ref name="Episode IX" />

Despite assumption, Bliss was able to escape before the [[destruction of Kijimi]], joining the Resistance and flying the ''Comeuppance'' alongside Babu Frik during the [[Battle of Exegol]] against the [[Sith Eternal military|Sith Eternal forces]]. The Resistance and their allies were ultimately victorious, following the demise of Sidious and the destruction of the ''Steadfast'', which stranded the remaining Sith Star Destroyers on Exegol.<ref name="Episode IX" />

Afterward, she joined the celebrations of the Resistance's victory back on [[Ajan Kloss]]. She and Dameron acknowledged each other during the celebration from across the crowds of Resistance members.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:ZoriiBliss-SWE-DK.png|thumb|right|150px|Zorii Bliss]]
Zorii Bliss was a [[human]] female<ref name="Episode IX" /> who, like her fellow Spice Runners, was considered a scoundrel.<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|zorii-bliss|Zorii Bliss}}</ref> Nonetheless, she developed a romantic relationship with Poe Dameron during his time with the group, only for Dameron's morals to later lead him to side against the Spice Runners during Bliss's mother's plot to kill rival families under the pretense of a summit. Bliss was also opposed to her mother but wanted to take over the Spice Runners with Dameron at her side. Upon hearing him reject her offer, Dameron observed that the affection and warmth she had felt towards him instantly crumbled away to rage, believing it would never return,<ref name="Free Fall" /> although the two later shared several close moments after reuniting.<ref name="Episode IX" />

Bliss had a unique and deadly fighting style due to her skill and background in dancing. Following her rise as leader of the Spice Runners, Bliss was feared by her enemies and respected by her fellow pirates.<ref name="2024 Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref>

==Equipment==
[[File:ZoriiBlissHelmet-CGSWG.png|thumb|left|200px|right|Zorii Bliss' helmet]]
By the time of the First Order's occupation of Kijimi, Bliss was equipped with a temperature-regulating [[Color|maroon]] [[body glove]] [[Flight suit]].<ref name="2024 Encyclopedia" /> Zorii was armed with a [[Zorii Bliss's blasters|pair]] of [[E-851 blaster pistol]]s<ref name="TROSVD" /> which she kept in a holster of hardened [[Bantha]]-[[leather]]<ref name="2024 Encyclopedia" />

Bliss hid her voice with a [[Vocabulator|vocoder]] in [[Zorii Bliss's helmet|her]] custom helmet that held technology within its [[plasteel]] shell meant to give an upper hand in combat topped with a [[bronzium]] finish.<ref name="2024 Encyclopedia" /> Bliss also came to buy a Y-wing she named the ''Comeuppance'',<ref name="TROS Expanded" /> with which she intended to escape Kijimi for the Colonies before instead using it to fight the Final Order in the Battle of Exegol.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Behind the scenes==
Zorii Bliss appeared in the [[2019]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], where she was portrayed by [[Keri Russell]].<ref name="Episode IX" /> Russell accepted the part because she found the idea of an anonymous, mysterious side character attractive.<ref name="Town & Country">{{WebCite|url=https://www.townandcountrymag.com/leisure/arts-and-culture/a29825639/keri-russell-star-wars-rise-of-skywalker-interview-2019|text=Keri Russell Is the Secret Force Behind ''Star Wars''|date=2019-11-25|work=[[Wikipedia:Town & Country (magazine)|Town & Country]]|archivedate=20200220145258}}</ref>

